WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.120 --> 00:00:06.210
After nearly four years, a wealth of action,
an array of crazy costumes, and, best of all,

00:00:06.210 --> 00:00:11.969
an abundance of phenomenal actors giving Suzanne
Collins' novels new life on the big screen,

00:00:11.969 --> 00:00:15.070
The Hunger Games franchise is finally coming
to an end.

00:00:15.070 --> 00:00:20.920
So, I wanted to look back over the most heart-in-your-mouth
moments from the final film, Mockingjay Part

00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:24.240
2.
Obviously, spoilers ahead if you haven't seen

00:00:24.240 --> 00:00:27.539
the film already!
And if that's you, I've got a non-spoiler

00:00:27.539 --> 00:00:29.340
review for you right here.

00:00:29.340 --> 00:00:34.370
Kicking off with number 5, Katniss hasn't
even made it to the Capitol to confront Snow,

00:00:34.370 --> 00:00:39.100
when she finds her life under threat.
She's trying to rally District 2's loyalists

00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:42.969
to the rebel cause, and let's just say they're
not exactly down with what the Mockingjay

00:00:42.969 --> 00:00:46.200
has to say.
Probably didn't put them in the best of moods

00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:49.710
that the rebels had just bombed them and caused
a bunch of avalanches.

00:00:49.710 --> 00:00:54.250
And just as one District 2 man relents after
putting a gun to Katniss's throat, another

00:00:54.250 --> 00:00:58.219
takes aim and hits his target.
Thank goodness for that bullet-proof outfit,

00:00:58.219 --> 00:00:59.219
hey?!

00:00:59.219 --> 00:01:04.510
At number 4, ok, so even if you haven't read
the novels, just hearing Boggs tell Katniss

00:01:04.510 --> 00:01:08.729
that he's not gonna let her die on his watch
leaves you feeling he wasn't long for this

00:01:08.729 --> 00:01:11.909
world!
And tragically, he's blown up just after Katniss

00:01:11.909 --> 00:01:17.049
and her squad survive an especially nasty
gun trap, one of the many hellish hidden traps

00:01:17.049 --> 00:01:20.509
that make the Capitol itself feel like a big
Hunger Games arena.

00:01:20.509 --> 00:01:25.020
But things go from bad to worse when the next
pod kicks off with what in the movie looks

00:01:25.020 --> 00:01:30.250
like a shockingly real wave of liquid tar
or crude oil that hits the courtyard like

00:01:30.250 --> 00:01:35.619
a Tsunami, forcing Katniss and co to run for
their lives to the top floor of a nearby building.

00:01:35.619 --> 00:01:39.950
Then most of them only just get away from
that building before Snow's troops arrive

00:01:39.950 --> 00:01:43.590
and completely obliterate it!
Talk about tense!

00:01:43.590 --> 00:01:48.850
Moving on to number 3, if you're not a fan
of confined spaces, then Pollux's suggestion

00:01:48.850 --> 00:01:53.790
that Katniss and her crew go underground quite
likely sent a shiver down your spine.

00:01:53.790 --> 00:01:59.439
And, oh my goodness, when I saw Pollux crawl
on his stomach through that tiny gap as they

00:01:59.439 --> 00:02:03.560
made their way through the tunnels, I swear
I felt my stomach turn over.

00:02:03.560 --> 00:02:09.149
And as if the tunnels aren't creepy and claustrophobic
enough as it is, there's also a load of lizard

00:02:09.149 --> 00:02:14.379
mutts thrown into the mix for some insanely
heart-stopping scenes which reminded me of

00:02:14.379 --> 00:02:17.430
both Aliens and the British horror movie The
Descent.

00:02:17.430 --> 00:02:21.170
As for the look of those monstrous mutts,
their design made me think of the sort of

00:02:21.170 --> 00:02:24.599
beasts created by Pan's Labyrinth director
Guillermo del Toro.

00:02:24.599 --> 00:02:29.760
Watching Katniss and her squad do battle with
those mutts in close quarters was quite something:

00:02:29.760 --> 00:02:34.110
there was Gale shooting them in the head,
and Finnick with his trident, to name just

00:02:34.110 --> 00:02:36.940
two.
Speaking of Finnick, the sound of his repeated

00:02:36.940 --> 00:02:41.510
screams for Katniss as he was beset by the
mutts was really chilling.

00:02:41.510 --> 00:02:46.450
And what about Katniss putting Finnick out
of his misery by detonating the Holo! Oh,

00:02:46.450 --> 00:02:47.450
man!

00:02:47.450 --> 00:02:52.250
And at number 2, In Mockingjay Part 1, you
could already see that President Coin was

00:02:52.250 --> 00:02:56.610
a cool and calculating cookie.
But she took that to an horrific extreme in

00:02:56.610 --> 00:03:01.800
Part 2 when she tricked Katniss, Snow, and
the people of Panem into thinking that Snow

00:03:01.800 --> 00:03:07.170
was the one who dropped those exploding parachutes
and bombed the rebel medics, when it was actually

00:03:07.170 --> 00:03:10.830
her.
And like that wasn't enough, Coin declared

00:03:10.830 --> 00:03:15.550
herself interim President of Panem – and
we all know just how long her kind of interim

00:03:15.550 --> 00:03:20.970
would have lasted –, plus, she wanted to
bring back the games… just “symbolic Hunger

00:03:20.970 --> 00:03:24.900
Games… in lieu of barbaric executions”,
as she put it.

00:03:24.900 --> 00:03:29.371
But as Katniss realised, it was a case of
plus ça change in Panem; in other words,

00:03:29.371 --> 00:03:33.310
all they'd done was to swap a white-haired
dictator for a grey-haired one!

00:03:33.310 --> 00:03:39.090
So, when the moment came to step up and execute
Snow, Katniss chose to shoot her arrow into

00:03:39.090 --> 00:03:44.319
President Coin instead, freeing Panem from
Coin's dictatorship before it really began

00:03:44.319 --> 00:03:49.790
and, at the same time, avenging Prim's death.
And let's not forget Coin's attempt to kill

00:03:49.790 --> 00:03:53.900
Katniss as well, for example by sending a
still-traumatised Peeta out to the Capitol

00:03:53.900 --> 00:03:58.210
with Katniss's squad.
Coin thought she was so clever, didn't she?

00:03:58.210 --> 00:04:04.040
And she was arrogant to the very last with
her line, ‘May your aim be as true as your

00:04:04.040 --> 00:04:05.420
heart is pure'.

00:04:05.420 --> 00:04:10.349
And at number 1, it was Katniss Everdeen's
desire to protect her sister that saw her

00:04:10.349 --> 00:04:15.030
volunteer to take Prim's place when she was
picked as District 12's tribute back in the

00:04:15.030 --> 00:04:18.790
first Hunger Games movie.
And, ultimately, it was that very personal

00:04:18.790 --> 00:04:23.960
desire that set Katniss on the road to become
the Mockingjay, a very public symbol of rebellion

00:04:23.960 --> 00:04:27.880
against the Capitol.
So, what a terrible irony it was that, in

00:04:27.880 --> 00:04:32.360
the end, Katniss could not save both the people
of Panem and her own sister.

00:04:32.360 --> 00:04:37.490
And the whole way it played out was just heart-breaking,
beginning with Snow's offer of shelter to

00:04:37.490 --> 00:04:41.790
the refugees and their children, to his troops
taking their kids away from them at the gates

00:04:41.790 --> 00:04:46.600
of his mansion, to the hovercrafts dropping
little parachutes like the ones sent to tributes

00:04:46.600 --> 00:04:52.530
during the Games, except these parachutes
were bombs not medicine or food, to finally,

00:04:52.530 --> 00:04:57.820
the rebel medics rushing in, Katniss seeing
Prim, calling out and walking towards her,

00:04:57.820 --> 00:05:03.289
only for a second wave of delayed bombs to
go off, killing Prim and blowing Katniss backwards,

00:05:03.289 --> 00:05:09.020
turning her into a literal girl on fire.
The whole thing was truly horrifying.

00:05:09.020 --> 00:05:12.720
Now, what are the moments that shocked you
most in Mockingjay Part 2?

00:05:12.720 --> 00:05:14.860
And what are your favourite scenes in the
movie?

